    "narrative": "Our offensive engine for July 22 is headlined by **Tyler Soderstrom**, whose 76.91 projection makes him the day's anchor. Facing Merrill Kelly and his inflated 5.31 xERA, **Soderstrom** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill boost and an ideal #2 spot in the order. He is joined in the elite tier by **James Wood** (71.14) and **Mickey Moniak** (69.64). Both outfielders draw significant park factors (+14%) and favorable matchups against Hughes and Cavalli, respectively. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (67.14) also stands out; while a 5% wind-in penalty drags his total slightly, his dominant 14% platoon edge against Roupp secures his place as our premier corner infielder for the day.\n\nDecisions in the middle of the pack were dictated by our internal mandate to prioritize stolen base potential and efficiency. **Jose Caballero** (57.58) and **Brice Turang** (55.97) represent high-floor plays, with **Caballero** drawing a notable 18% boost against the vulnerable M. Keller. On the bench, **Josh Naylor** (59.86) presented the most difficult case; despite a solid projection, his poor BvP history against Singer and the superior efficiency ratings of our starting core kept him out of the daily lineup. We are closely monitoring the 35% rain risk surrounding **Austin Riley** (64.43) in his tilt against M. King; while his score remains strong, the weather could suppress his counting stats if the game is shortened or delayed.\n\nFinally, we are tracking confirmed lineups for **Isaac Paredes** and **Seiya Suzuki**, whose scores of 65.35 and 63.46 assume top-of-the-order usage. While **Corbin Carroll** (59.77) technically falls into the \"Strong\" category, his efficiency is currently hampered by an elite hold on the opposing battery, limiting his stolen base ceiling today against Jump. We are comfortable rolling out this configuration, prioritizing the high-upside matchups for **Soderstrom** and **Wood** while keeping our rostered depth, including **Zach McKinstry** and **Cole Young**, ready to rotate if pinch-hit opportunities emerge.",
